preConditionHook:
// TRAIL THE STOP INTO THE MOST RECENT MICRO MEASURING GAP. A bar whose low sits
// above the high of the bar TWO before it leaves a two-bar-apart gap that Brooks
// reads as a sign of strength; the stop goes just under it, and moves again each
// time a new gap prints. Mirrored for shorts on a bar whose high is below the low
// of two bars ago.
//
// The gap test itself is trivial; all the machinery is in HOLDING THE LAST GAP'S
// LEVEL, which is why the rule is carried whole rather than split -- as a stop it
// is the level that matters, not the bar.
//
// Not MicroMeasuringGap, the Entry: that one also requires the middle bar to be a
// trend bar of a given body fraction and uses the INCLUSIVE boundary
// low[0] >= high[2], where this follows its own source's STRICT low[0] > high[2],
// so the two differ on an exact touch. Not LimitEntryAtMicroGapEdge, which is a
// limit entry at the gap edge one bar later.
//
// A STALE LEVEL CANNOT TAKE A NEW TRADE OFF. The gap is market structure, not
// position state, so the level survives across trades -- but a bull gap left far
// above a later entry would fire on the fill bar. At entry the level is therefore
// armed only if it sits at or below that bar's close (mirrored for shorts), and a
// gap that prints during the trade arms it unconditionally, since such a level is
// at or below its own bar's close by construction. Armed with
// ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0, VERIFIED as 0 on the fill bar and as restarting
// through a reversal, which a ctx.MarketPosition() == 0 reset would miss because a
// reversal never passes through flat. The arming is a bool rather than the merged
// pseudocode's gapLevel > 0 test, because a back-adjusted continuous contract can
// price below zero.
//
// Ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is written division-first,
// toleranceTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), into a local.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 2.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    useGapLong = gapSeenLong && el_le(gapLong, close[0]);
    useGapShort = gapSeenShort && el_ge(gapShort, close[0]);
}
if (el_gt(low[0], high[2])) {
    gapLong = low[0];
    gapSeenLong = true;
    useGapLong = true;
}
if (el_lt(high[0], low[2])) {
    gapShort = high[0];
    gapSeenShort = true;
    useGapShort = true;
}
